{"key":"bsd-3-clause","name":"BSD 3-Clause \"New\" or \"Revised\" License","spdx_id":"BSD-3-Clause","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/bsd-3-clause","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTU="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["framework","hacktoberfest","php","php-framework","yii","yii2"],"visibility":"public","forks":6857,"open_issues":521,"watchers":14308,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"I upgraded to the latest Yii2 release and updated my code for the new `changedAttributes` parameter in afterSave().\n\nStrangely, some of my unit tests (which used to work before the upgrade) started throwing this error, regarding a column named `token` in my model:\n\n``` php\nyii\\base\\ErrorException: Undefined index: token\n#1 /srv/dev/project/vendor/yiisoft/yii2/db/BaseActiveRecord.php:719\n```\n\nMind you: this is not a validation error, but an exception due to the `$this->_oldAttributes` array not containing an item named `token`.\nIn this particular situation, an existing record (with token = null) is being updated.\n\nI was able to fix this issue by adding this line to my model's validation rules:\n\n``` php\n['token', 'default', 'value' => null],\n```\n\nHowever, I would like to understand the underlying cause. Should I add the default value rule for every attribute from now on? Or is this a bug that causes fields with value null to be skipped in the `$this->_oldAttributes` array?\n\nI guess this might be related to @dizews 44f20c61a012b63f18b2408512adf26f5e009dd4 commit\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yiisoft/yii2/issues/4150/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yiisoft/yii2/issues/4150/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.gith